    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Michael Gilmartin are delighted to bring this exceptional architecturally designed home at Ballyscanlon, Coolbawn, Co. Tipperary to the market.\n\nOffering stunning views over the surrounding countryside and Lough Derg, this impressive residence measures approximately 269 sqm and is certainly not your typical home. Beautifully presented throughout, the property combines generous accommodation with an abundance of natural light and an enviable setting.\n\nThe heart of the home is a superb open-plan living, kitchen and dining area, featuring a spacious layout and large windows which take full advantage of the stunning countryside and lake views.\n\nThere is also a large, light filled reception room with a vaulted ceiling and Velux windows. This impressive space has a solid fuel stove and double doors opening directly onto the beautiful rear garden, creating an excellent connection between the indoor and outdoor living areas.\n\nThe ground floor is further complemented by a spacious en-suite double bedroom, along with an additional versatile area incorporating a bedroom, utility room, shower room and loft space.\n\nUpstairs are two further spacious double bedrooms, both of which are en-suite and benefit from walk-in wardrobes. The master bedroom is a particularly impressive space, featuring a private balcony area where the stunning views over Lough Derg can be enjoyed.\n\nThe property has a B energy rating and also benefits from an external sunroom, accessed from the kitchen, together with a patio area sheltered by a sandstone wall, providing an ideal space for outdoor entertaining and relaxation.\n\nThe location is equally impressive. Situated within easy reach of both Nenagh and Portumna, the property is close to the shores of Lough Derg and a number of popular access points and amenities, including Luska, Kilgarvan and Terryglass.\n\nThis is a unique and beautifully presented home which offers spacious, versatile accommodation in an outstanding location with magnificent lake and countryside views.\n\nViewing of this exceptional property is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 1.4w x 1.1\n\n\nEntrance Hall - 1.4156w x 7.865d\n\n\nOpen Plan Kitchen/Living/Dining - 6.229w x 8.064d\nFully tiled, fitted kitchen, integrated 4 ring gas hob, electric oven, integrated dishwasher. French doors to side\n\nBack Hall - 4.674w x 1.948d\nTiled, panelling on wall\n\nUtility Room - 3.881w x 3.765d\nSink, plumbed for washing machine\n\nLiving Room - 5.035w x 7.809d\nVaulted ceiling, solid fuel stove, french double doors to garden\n\nBedroom 1/Study with Galley Area - 3.866w x 3.723d\nTiled\n\nGalley Area - 3.885w x 3.795d\n\n\nWet Room - 1.869w x 0.800d\nTiled\n\nBack Porch - 2.268w x 1.356d\nTimber floor\n\nDownstairs Bedroom 2 - 3.804w x 3.907d\n\n\nEnsuite Wet Room - 2.232w x 1.630d\n\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.565w x 1.264d\n\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.962w x 3.783d\nTimber floor, built in wardrobe\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 2.579w x 1.224d\n\n\nBedroom 4 - 8.655w x 5.659d\nWalk in Wardrobe and Ensuite\n\nWalk in Wardrobe and Ensuite - 2.543w x 1.929d\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Detached house overlooking Lough Derg.</li><li> Spacious accommodation.</li><li> Ground floor bedroom with en-suite.</li><li> Solar panels.</li><li> Solid fuel stove</li><li> 2 first floor en-suite bedrooms.</li><li> Master bedroom also has French doors to balcony to capture the view.</li><li> Underfloor heating on ground floor</li><li> South Westerly Facing Rear Garden</li><li> Services: Oil Fired Central Heating, Group Water Scheme and Septic Tank</li><li> c.269sqm</ul>"
